---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Penguin-Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';

const currentDate = new Date();
let currentYear = currentDate.getFullYear();
---

<Layout title="Penguins">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
		<title>Penguins</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<header class="header">
        	<h1>Chinstrap Penguin</h1>
    	</header>
		<Navbar/>
        <main>
            <div class="container">
                <nav class="contents">
                    <h2>Contents:</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#diet">Diet</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#behavior">Social Behavior</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#facts">Facts</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>
                
                <section id="overview">
                    <h2>Overview</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Scientific Name: Pygoscelis antarctica</li>
                        <li>Size: Medium-sized penguins, standing 70–75 cm (28–30 inches) tall and weighing 3.5–6 kg (7.7–13.2 lb).</li>
                        <li>Habitat: Breed on rocky coasts of Antarctica and surrounding islands.</li>
                        <li>Conservation Status: Least Concern (IUCN)</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <section id="diet">
                    <h2>Diet</h2>
                    <p>Chinstrap penguins are krill specialists, feeding primarily on these tiny crustaceans. They also consume small fish, squid, and other marine invertebrates.  These birds are excellent swimmers, using their powerful flippers to propel themselves through the water at high speeds.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="behavior">
                    <h2>Social Behavior</h2>
                    <p>Chinstrap penguins form large breeding colonies, sometimes reaching hundreds of thousands of individuals.  They are monogamous birds, forming pairs that cooperate in building nests, incubating eggs, and raising chicks.  These penguins are known for their aggressive behavior, often defending their nests and territories from other birds.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="facts">
                    <h2>Interesting Facts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Chinstrap penguins have a distinctive black band that runs under their chin, giving them their name.</li>
                        <li>These penguins are known for their loud vocalizations, often heard as a cacophony of calls and squawks.</li>
                        <li>Chinstrap penguins are an important food source for predators such as leopard seals and killer whales.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p><span class="copyleft">&copy;</span> PengiCoder & MrPiggy105, { currentYear }</p>
            </footer>
        </main>
	</body>
</Layout>

<style>
    .contents ul {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .contents li {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    section {
        overflow: hidden;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        margin-left: 30%;
    }

    h1{
        text-align: center;
        height: 100%;
        font-family: 'Orkney', Arial;
    }
</style>
